Z||000014||batboy||04-30-2000||04:49 PM||||This ain't no joke, I'm being serious. Last month, while I was driving my Blazer that's assigned to me at work, I almost accidently got tangled up into a police chase. Some guy took a GMC pickup for a test drive off a car lot and robbed a bank in a small town called Rossville near Topeka, KS (maybe Dogtired or PHerd might remember hearing about this). For a split second I had the opportunity to block the suspect's escape as he attempted to cross the highway I was on (he had to slow down for me because I was in the way). Lots of things flashed through my mind in that amount of time, like he might try and ram me and that he probably had a gun. I decided to let the half dozen police cars chasing him earn their pay and got the hell out of there. After a 20 mile chase at speeds in excess of 100 MPH, the guy crashed into a tree and was caught. It sure was exciting to see a real full blown chase in progress though (what little bit I saw anyway).||||reg||1
